00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.840
Let us look at one easy grammar pattern.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:16.420
Russian use the verb stanovicia when something changes and becomes a new state.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.400
It is like English saying it is getting warm or it is turning green.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:25.880
We simply say stanovicia plus the describing word.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.200
stanovicia Тепло.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:29.900
It becomes warm.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:33.460
Весной stanovicia зелено.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.280
In spring it becomes green.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:37.060
Летом stanovicia зарко.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.500
In summer it becomes hot.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:40.880
Listen again.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.580
stanovicia Тепло.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.100
stanovicia Тепло.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:50.420
